WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.767
Sunlight carries energy in tiny packets called photons.

2
00:00:04.817 --> 00:00:08.391
This is how a solar panel turns them into electricity.

3
00:00:09.291 --> 00:00:13.467
When a photon hits the silicon, it knocks an electron loose.

4
00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:20.504
The cell's built-in electric field pushes those electrons one way, and that flow is a current.

5
00:00:21.504 --> 00:00:23.660
Panels produce direct current.

6
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.770
An inverter switches it to alternating current, the kind your home runs on.

7
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.933
Output follows the sun.

8
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:36.950
It climbs through the morning, peaks around midday, and fades by evening.

